    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.extra\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nI wanted to browse the new files created in the repo.\r\n\r\n`:Pick git_files scope=\"untracked\"` shows untracked files along with ignored files. This is because the only argument that get's passed in that case is `--others`.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n  local args = ({\r\n    tracked = { '--cached' },\r\n    modified = { '--modified' },\r\n    untracked = { '--others' },\r\n    ignored = { '--others', '--ignored', '--exclude-standard' },\r\n    deleted = { '--deleted' },\r\n  })[local_opts.scope]\r\n```\r\n\r\n`:Pick git_files scope=\"ignored\"` has similar behavior to `scope=\"untracked\"` as far as I can see right now.\r\n\r\n`untracked` needs to have `--exclude-standard` so that ignored files don't show up in the results, I think?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.extra</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I wanted to browse the new files created in the repo.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick git_files scope=\"untracked\"</code> shows untracked files along with ignored files. This is because the only argument that get's passed in that case is <code class=\"notranslate\">--others</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"  local args = ({\n    tracked = { '--cached' },\n    modified = { '--modified' },\n    untracked = { '--others' },\n    ignored = { '--others', '--ignored', '--exclude-standard' },\n    deleted = { '--deleted' },\n  })[local_opts.scope]\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> ({\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">tracked</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>--cached<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">modified</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>--modified<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">untracked</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>--others<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">ignored</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>--others<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>--ignored<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>--exclude-standard<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">deleted</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>--deleted<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n  })[<span class=\"pl-smi\">local_opts</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">scope</span>]</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick git_files scope=\"ignored\"</code> has similar behavior to <code class=\"notranslate\">scope=\"untracked\"</code> as far as I can see right now.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">untracked</code> needs to have <code class=\"notranslate\">--exclude-standard</code> so that ignored files don't show up in the results, I think?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.extra\nQuestion\nI wanted to browse the new files created in the repo.\n:Pick git_files scope=\"untracked\" shows untracked files along with ignored files. This is because the only argument that get's passed in that case is --others.\n  local args = ({\n    tracked = { '--cached' },\n    modified = { '--modified' },\n    untracked = { '--others' },\n    ignored = { '--others', '--ignored', '--exclude-standard' },\n    deleted = { '--deleted' },\n  })[local_opts.scope]\n:Pick git_files scope=\"ignored\" has similar behavior to scope=\"untracked\" as far as I can see right now.\nuntracked needs to have --exclude-standard so that ignored files don't show up in the results, I think?",
