            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> `:Pick git_files scope=\"untracked\"` shows untracked files along with ignored files. This is because the only argument that get's passed in that case is `--others`.\r\n\r\n*Technically*, this is a [documented behavior](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/44657837c7338e52727facc85c1d95bec1f6bd7c/doc/mini-extra.txt#L441). The ignored files are (in some sense) not tracked. But yeah, I agree that there needs to be a way to pick only \"added\" files.\r\n\r\n> `:Pick git_files scope=\"ignored\"` has similar behavior to `scope=\"untracked\"` as far as I can see right now.\r\n\r\nNot quite, as it doesn't show purely \"added\" files.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'll take a look.",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick git_files scope=\"untracked\"</code> shows untracked files along with ignored files. This is because the only argument that get's passed in that case is <code class=\"notranslate\">--others</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Technically</em>, this is a <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/44657837c7338e52727facc85c1d95bec1f6bd7c/doc/mini-extra.txt#L441\">documented behavior</a>. The ignored files are (in some sense) not tracked. But yeah, I agree that there needs to be a way to pick only \"added\" files.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick git_files scope=\"ignored\"</code> has similar behavior to <code class=\"notranslate\">scope=\"untracked\"</code> as far as I can see right now.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Not quite, as it doesn't show purely \"added\" files.</p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'll take a look.</p>",
            "bodyText": ":Pick git_files scope=\"untracked\" shows untracked files along with ignored files. This is because the only argument that get's passed in that case is --others.\n\nTechnically, this is a documented behavior. The ignored files are (in some sense) not tracked. But yeah, I agree that there needs to be a way to pick only \"added\" files.\n\n:Pick git_files scope=\"ignored\" has similar behavior to scope=\"untracked\" as far as I can see right now.\n\nNot quite, as it doesn't show purely \"added\" files.\n\nI'll take a look.",
