            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "After having some time to reconsider, I do now think that `scope=\"untracked\"` was meant to act like described here. I.e. it should show only untracked files that are meant to be tracked.\r\n\r\nThis should now be fixed on the latest `main`. Thanks for bringing this up!",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">After having some time to reconsider, I do now think that <code class=\"notranslate\">scope=\"untracked\"</code> was meant to act like described here. I.e. it should show only untracked files that are meant to be tracked.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This should now be fixed on the latest <code class=\"notranslate\">main</code>. Thanks for bringing this up!</p>",
            "bodyText": "After having some time to reconsider, I do now think that scope=\"untracked\" was meant to act like described here. I.e. it should show only untracked files that are meant to be tracked.\nThis should now be fixed on the latest main. Thanks for bringing this up!",
